{
  "id": "flashattention_3_breakdown",
  "title": "FlashAttention-3: Asynchronous Hardware Parallelism",
  "category": "architecture_breakdown",
  "domain_taxonomy": "neural_attention",
  "hook_tag": "MEMORY LATENCY KILLED",
  "beats": [
    {
      "beat_id": 1,
      "text": "Your H100s are idling like bored construction workers, waiting for memory to arrive from the HBM.",
      "visual_focus": "Split screen showing an H100 chip glowing red versus a stagnant memory bus.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "idling": "#EF4444"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "HBM Latency",
        "action_verb": "starves",
        "direct_object": "Tensor Cores",
        "anchor_word": "idling",
        "semantic_role": "state_transition"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "grid_memory",
        "title": "THE IDLE PARADOX",
        "sub": "Compute vs Memory",
        "accent_color": "#EF4444",
        "params": {
          "grid_title": "GPU HBM Access Map",
          "active_cell_label": "Memory Stall",
          "efficiency_label": "Low Bandwidth Utilization"
        }
      },
      "thriller_role": "pattern_interrupt_hook",
      "act": 1
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 2,
      "text": "The villain is HBM latency. Your math units sit empty because the data isn't ready; it's a relay race failure.",
      "visual_focus": "Animation of a runner stopping dead in their tracks while waiting for a baton.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "relay race failure": "#EF4444"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Memory Latency",
        "action_verb": "blocks",
        "direct_object": "Throughput",
        "anchor_word": "failure",
        "semantic_role": "bottleneck_identification"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "split_flow",
        "title": "THE RELAY BOTTLENECK",
        "sub": "Data starvation",
        "accent_color": "#EF4444",
        "params": {}
      },
      "thriller_role": "villain_bottleneck",
      "act": 2
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 3,
      "text": "FlashAttention-3 introduces Asynchronous Tiling. It breaks the deadlock by overlapping memory fetches with active computation, hiding the latency entirely.",
      "visual_focus": "Overlapping bars showing memory load and compute happening simultaneously.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "Asynchronous Tiling": "#22C55E"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Asynchronous Tiling",
        "action_verb": "overlaps",
        "direct_object": "Memory and Compute",
        "anchor_word": "deadlock",
        "semantic_role": "solution_pivot"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "split_flow",
        "title": "ASYNCHRONOUS TILING",
        "sub": "Parallel execution",
        "accent_color": "#34D399",
        "params": {
          "input_label": "Data stream",
          "router_label": "Async Scheduler",
          "branch_a_label": "HBM Fetch",
          "branch_a_sub": "Non-blocking",
          "branch_b_label": "Tensor Core",
          "branch_b_sub": "Active Compute"
        }
      },
      "thriller_role": "eureka_mechanism",
      "act": 3
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 4,
      "text": "Using CUDA pipelines, it schedules memory loads for the next block while the current block is still crunching numbers on the Tensor Cores.",
      "visual_focus": "Code block showing pipeline scheduling logic.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "CUDA pipelines": "#22C55E"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "CUDA pipelines",
        "action_verb": "schedules",
        "direct_object": "Data blocks",
        "anchor_word": "crunching",
        "semantic_role": "technical_mechanism"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "attention_prism_refraction",
        "title": "PIPELINE SCHEDULING",
        "sub": "Hiding latency",
        "accent_color": "#F59E0B",
        "params": {
          "token_label": "Block (64x64)",
          "matrix_title": "Tiled Accumulation"
        }
      },
      "thriller_role": "technical_deep_dive",
      "act": 3
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 5,
      "text": "The result? A massive 1.2 TFLOPS throughput, delivering an 81% performance jump over the previous version.",
      "visual_focus": "Bar chart showing a massive spike in performance metrics.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "81% performance jump": "#22C55E"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "FlashAttention-3",
        "action_verb": "achieves",
        "direct_object": "1.2 TFLOPS",
        "anchor_word": "jump",
        "semantic_role": "empirical_payoff"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "horizontal_race_bars",
        "title": "81% PERFORMANCE GAIN",
